<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khitans</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Khitan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khitans were a nomadic people of the Mongolian and Manchurian steppe who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in the tenth century. Earlier they had been among the peoples subject to or neighbouring the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Gokturk Empire</a>. The Khitan Liao state was a major rival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a>, which paid it annual tribute to maintain peace.</p></div>
